From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:33:36 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: account for NV12 flicker replies in tuning
 tests

The preview fixture describes P010, whose flicker request has no output.
The new tuning failure cases use NV12, whose existing flicker request
returns a 12-byte record. Keep both expectations in the shared transport
stub so the tests validate the appropriate command ABI.

Clarify that a completed tuning upload is a transport result rather than
proof that the firmware applied every coefficient; its NV12 reply fields
remain undecoded.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0ab62d2f77797be2f5b375d2fb2545fcb49f4084)
---
 Documentation/driver-api/media/drivers/apple-isp-j616s.rst | 2 ++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam-test.c            | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/driver-api/media/drivers/apple-isp-j616s.rst b/Documentation/driver-api/media/drivers/apple-isp-j616s.rst
index e393dfb6a8..c119fc86f5 100644
--- a/Documentation/driver-api/media/drivers/apple-isp-j616s.rst
+++ b/Documentation/driver-api/media/drivers/apple-isp-j616s.rst
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@ only to the copied firmware buffer. A missing file allows streaming with a
 warning. An invalid file, interrupted read or failed firmware upload fails
 stream setup instead of silently continuing. A debug message identifies a
 successful upload without dumping its contents.
+This confirms transport completion only: the NV12 path does not decode the
+setfile reply fields, so it does not prove that every coefficient was applied.
 
 The NV12 command sequence already sends ``CH_CNR_START`` (0x0a2f),
 ``CH_MBNR_ENABLE`` (0x0a3a, use case 0, mode 1, chroma enabled),
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam-test.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam-test.c
index 58e3df1e0f..f0be0f0fb2 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam-test.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam-test.c
@@ -79,6 +79,7 @@ static int isp_test_send(struct apple_isp *isp, void *args, u32 insize,
 	struct kunit *test = kunit_get_current_test();
 	struct isp_test_command_trace *trace = test->priv;
 	const struct isp_test_command *expected;
+	u32 expected_outsize;
 
 	if (trace->count >= ARRAY_SIZE(isp_test_preview_commands)) {
 		KUNIT_FAIL(test, "unexpected extra command");
@@ -86,7 +87,9 @@ static int isp_test_send(struct apple_isp *isp, void *args, u32 insize,
 	}
 	expected = &isp_test_preview_commands[trace->count++];
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, insize, expected->size);
-	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, outsize, expected->words[1] == 0x117 ? insize : 0);
+	expected_outsize = expected->words[1] == 0x117 ||
+		(expected->words[1] == 0x24 && !isp_is_p010(isp)) ? insize : 0;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, outsize, expected_outsize);
 	if (insize == expected->size)
 		KUNIT_EXPECT_MEMEQ(test, args, expected->words, insize);
 	if (trace->count == trace->fail_at)
